Appendix H. Coupling Matrix and DoF Mapping

H.1 Coupling Matrix

The tendon-to-joint torque map is

\tau_{\text{joint}} = C^T(q) \tau,

with C^T(q) \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times n}. For the underactuated finger with 3 joints and 1 tendon,

C_{\text{finger}}^T(q) =
\begin{bmatrix}
r_1(q) & r_2(q) & r_3(q)
\end{bmatrix},

where r_i(q) is the moment arm of the tendon about joint i. The moment arm is configuration-dependent:

r_i(q) = \frac{\partial L_{\text{tendon}}}{\partial q_i}.

H.2 DoF/Motor/Tendon Mapping

