Appendix J. Calibration Drift Protocol

J.1 Protocol

1. Baseline calibration at n_g = 0.
2. After n_g = 1000 grasps: measure reconstruction error on a reference object.
3. After n_g = 3300 grasps: repeat.
4. Apply online brightness and contrast adjustment after each measurement.
5. Compare reconstruction error before and after adjustment.

J.2 Metrics

E_{\text{rec}}(n_g) = \frac{1}{|\mathcal{P}|} \sum_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \|z_T(p) - \hat{z}_T(p; n_g)\|^2,

where \mathcal{P} is the set of test points and \hat{z}_T(p; n_g) is the reconstruction after n_g grasps.

J.3 Falsifiable Prediction

The calibration drift of the prototype should satisfy

\frac{E_{\text{rec}}(3300)}{E_{\text{rec}}(0)} \leq 1.2,

following the GelSlim benchmark. If the drift exceeds this threshold, the internal forearm camera must compensate by providing an independent tendon-length estimate.

