Appendix K. Statistical Power and Falsifiability

K.1 Primary Endpoint

The primary endpoint is the occlusion-conditioned localization error

E_{\text{loc}} = \mathbb{E}\left[\|\hat{p} - p\|^2 \mid M = 0\right].

K.2 Power Analysis

Assume a 20% reduction in E_{\text{loc}} with standard deviation \sigma = 0.5 \bar{E}. For power 1 - \beta = 0.8 and significance \alpha = 0.05, the required sample size per group is

n_{\text{trials}} = \frac{2 (z_{1-\alpha/2} + z_{1-\beta})^2 \sigma^2}{\Delta^2} = \frac{2 (1.96 + 0.84)^2 \times 0.25}{0.04} \approx 98.

We therefore require n_{\text{trials}} \geq 100 per condition.

K.3 Falsifiability

The proposition is falsified if:

1. \operatorname{rank} \mathcal{O}_{\text{dist}} - \operatorname{rank} \mathcal{O}_{\text{ext}} = 0 under occlusion;
2. \Delta I_{\text{occ}} \leq 0;
3. the ablation removing internal perception produces no significant drop in task success;
4. the prototype fails to beat Baseline A by 20% on the primary endpoint at equal mass.

